{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And he shall make her swear, etc.</b> And what is the oath? 'If no man has lain with you' — you are clear. But if a man has lain with you — [you are guilty]. For when he spells out the negative, you do not hear the affirmative — but the rule is to open capital cases with the case for acquittal (ibid. 17; Shevuot 36; Sanhedrin 33)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:31.776469564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}